Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 04:05:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(maestro): cancelled closed terminal +
 TaskLedger.cancelSession (0.76.0, BPT P0-D1)

A user-initiated cancel is now a first-class terminal outcome, ledger-
distinguishable from 'failed' and never auto-rerun (the two non-negotiable
semantic lines of BPT requirement P0-D1, 2026-07-22).

- SessionState/SessionEvent: terminal 'cancelled' (no outgoing edges,
  appended LAST in SESSION_STATES) + 'cancel' event legal from every
  non-terminal state; TERMINAL_STATES includes it; state.ts mutation
  score holds the 100.00 ratchet floor (99 killed, 0 survived).
- TaskLedger.cancelSession(id, { reason?, cancelledAt? }): idempotent on
  cancelled, InvalidTransitionError on done/failed, per-session mutex +
  putSessionIf CAS with bounded re-read-re-apply on CAS loss; nextRunAt
  and leaseUntil cleared unconditionally (never due, never claimable,
  never swept).
- Query audit (P0-D1 4.4 option A): QueryOutcome gains 'cancelled';
  cancelling from running appends the in-flight attempt's epitaph row
  (error = reason); pending/retrying cancels append nothing;
  recordOutcome rejects 'cancelled' as an executor-reportable result.
- SessionRecord gains optional cancelledAt/cancelReason (pure additive;
  lastError not repurposed).
- Cancel-vs-attempt races pinned both ways; the driver silently drops
  the late result's InvalidTransitionError on a cancelled session (a
  user cancel is not a driver malfunction).
- Contract suite: new cancelled round-trip check (restart never
  resurrects a cancelled session).
- Lockstep 0.76.0 both packages (agent side: alignment line only).

Verification: maestro 362/362 (29 files, +20 cancel cases), testbed
30/30, agent 3216 passed, dep-direction OK, version guards OK, pack
dry-run OK, Stryker ledger-state 100.00.

